Z||000008||Slammed Fiero||07-04-2001||06:24 PM||||Ahh the buick has NO WHERE NEAR the technology of the Nissan Skyline GTR ...Read a book man , what kind of immature crap is "If you like Japenese cars move to Japan"<BR>the Skyline is a NEW car.<BR>?? My dad has a 911 , perhaps he should move to Germany??<P>Skyline:<P>2 Garett T3 turbo's running in paralell , each turbo runs off of 3 cylinders. Impellers in the turbo are ceramic coated (FROM THE FACTORY) <P>2.6ltrs 280hp stock. <P>Variable valve timing , all aluminum , ceramic coating used throughout , teflon coated pistons.<P><BR>Grand nationals were nice for thier time , but in the grand scheme of things they were a boring car with a big motor. They handled like shopping karts (GNX was better by a long shot)<P>But C'mon before you attempt to shoot down people , read a book. Turbo tech has come so far in the past few years it's not funny. There are several good turbo books out there. To get a basic idea try Reeves Callaway's book.<BR>I have run merkurs with 2.3ltr turbo's and a 66 corvair pushing 240hp from 2.9ltrs or turbo'd flat 6.<P>READ A BOOK<P><BR>I don't even know why I posted this , you sound a lot like "fierodude" in your assessment of japenese cars. I'm stayin out of this from now on. I don't think cliff needs any headaches from ignorant people who are just talking out their ass. <P>JM<BR>||||reg||1
