Z||000016||Predator||07-04-2001||08:29 PM||||I think everybody is entitled to their opinion of their cars, and insulting one just because you don't like it is not very nice. I had a 1971 Ford Torino Cobrajet, and some would say it was a land yacht, but I liked it, and it was fun to drive. I don't particularly want a 850 hp car to drive to work every day in. It's cool to look at, but I wouldn't want to pay the insurance for it. If we all liked the same exact cars then there would only be one manufacturer. There is no need to poke fun at other peoples cars just because you don't like it. If you keep things in perspective and look at the Grand National for what it was in the 80's then it has more than earned respect for it's time period, and I do agree as I have stated when people compare a Fiero to a new car. If I buy a 2001 anything it better have better technology in it then what was being produced in the mid 80's or I want my 20 to 40 something thousand dollars back so I can buy an 80's car for 5 or 6 grand.  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||7
