Z||000070||Will||07-07-2001||10:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Neal:<BR><B>No doubt that the GN is a sweet ride, but im gonna argue to the end the japanese engines are simply better.<BR>What is the most hi-tech american engine?<BR>probably the northstar.  right<BR>about 300hp & 300ft# (now i dont have the exact stats so correct me if im wrong)<BR>now broken down into hp/liter thats about 65hp per liter.<BR>Tell me the japanese arent doing MUCH better than that.  s2000 120hp/liter, new integra 95hp/liter...<P>Now just think what honda could do if they, GASP, worked their majic on a 350ci motor.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>The Northstar is a nine year old design (that's right, it came out in '92). The LS6 is GM's current technology centerpiece.<BR>The LS6 ECM uses a 32 bit processor.<BR>The LS6 has a aluminum block and heads.<BR>The LS6 has <I>cast in place</I> bay to bay breathing windows.<BR>The LS6 crank has gun drilled mains, also for bay-to-bay breathing.<BR>The LS6 ECM stays in <I>closed loop</I> operation at full throttle. It doesn't even use a wide band O2 sensor.<BR>The LS6 for '02 uses hollow valves, the exhaust valves filled with sodium/potassium mix.<BR>The LS1 architecture also has a host of other high end traits, like deep threaded head bolt holes, torque to yield bolts, six bolt main caps, etc., etc.<P>Don't give me this high specific output tripe.<BR>Ever heard of NASCAR? Those 350's, running restrictor plates, have specific outputs that would make VTEC engines sick. There's no high-tech in NASCAR, just good solid engine building.<P>Let's talk about the real indicator of high-tech design: specific torque--ftlbs per litre.<BR>Honda S2000: 2.0 litres, 153 ftlbs: 76.5 ftlbs per litre, using a 4 valve head and VTEC.<P>Chevrolet Corvette Z06 (2002): 5.66 litres, 400 ftlbs: 70.67 ftlbs per litre. Not bad for an engine using 2 valve heads and static valve timing.<P>The LS6 also has a lot of room for improvement:<BR>Does the S2000 use headers? yes<BR>Does the Corvette use headers? no<P>Where's the huge technology gap?<P>And don't forget that the Corvette, carrying around nearly three times the displacement of the S2000, beats the S2000 by 2 mpg on the highway.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000071||Neal||07-07-2001||11:30 PM||||Will, LS6 definitly sounds like it bridges the technology gap.  But look at what is in the rest of GM's line up now im not gonna bash any of it (I like GM) but look at what is in 90% of hondas line up and the technology, power per hp, and gas mileage are better.<P>And just for fun lets look at probably the MOST DESIREABLE 6cyl to date...<BR>BMW M3<BR>inline 6, 3.2 liters, 333hp, 262ft#<BR>thats 104 hp/liter and 82 ft#/liter<P>Now i think everyone here can agree BMW makes the BEST 6cyl||||reg||1
Z||000072||Sleeper||07-07-2001||11:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Will:<BR><B> "Hello, Apple? This is Orange. You suck."<P>Let's compare apples to apples.<BR>A 3.2 litre engine running 15 lbs of boost and spinning to 8500 RPM will output approximately twice the power of a similarly cammed, tuned, etc. 1.6 litre running 15 lbs of boost and spinning to 8500 RPM.<P>There is no replacement for displacement.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>it just flew right over your head...listen to JohnnyK, there IS replacement for displacement. my friend has a 66 nova with built 383 and my other friend has a 90 vw corrado 1.6L with a Garett T-3 turbo. theres like what, over 4 liter differance. they race all the time and the vw wins every time, not by much but it still a win and proves JohnnyK point.<P><BR>something else for import haters to look upon:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/radcrx.jpg">  <BR>2.2L's of vtec ALL MOTOR low 10 second excitement. <P>------------------<BR>85 GT Auto<BR>17" Racing Hart C5 wheels wrapped with Kumho Ecsta Supra 712 tires, Intrax lowering springs, KYB shocks, KYB-GR2 struts, West Coast Fiero Strut Tower Bar, West Coast Fiero Cold-Air Intake w/ HKS Super Flow filter, J.E.T. super chip and MSD Blaster Coil.||||reg||1
